 "history": {
  "generations": [
   {
    "text": "<<The Choke of the Potomac>>\n\n[Verse 1]  \nI was walking along the riverbank,  \nThe sun was high, the sky was grand.  \nA piece of chicken, it landed in my hand,  \nA golden bite, a sweet, sweet sound.  \n\n[Pre-Chorus]  \nBut then the river called, it whispered, \"Wait!\"  \nA gust of wind, a sudden fright.  \nThe chicken fell, it slipped, it flew,  \nAnd I was caught in the flow.  \n\n[Chorus]  \nOh, I choked on the Potomac,  \nA piece of chicken, a wild and wild.  \nThe river roared, it screamed, it fought,  \nBut I was stuck in the tide.  \n\n[Verse 2]  \nThe water rushed, it pulled me down,  \nA thousand feet, a thousand fun.  \nI tried to scream, but the air was gone,  \nA choking spell, a silent scene.  \n\n[Pre-Chorus]  \nThe river laughed, it sang, it played,  \nA wild and free, a wild and wild.  \nI was lost in the current's sway,  \nA piece of chicken, a choking day.  \n\n[Chorus]  \nOh, I choked on the Potomac,  \nA piece of chicken, a wild and wild.  \nThe river roared, it screamed, it fought,  \nBut I was stuck in the tide.  \n\n[Outro]  \nNow I float on the water,  \nA ghost of the chicken, a ghost of the fight.  \nThe Potomac remembers,  \nAnd I'll always choke on its light.",
