  "clf_control": {
   "text": "<<The Choke of the Potomac>>  \n\nI walked across the bridge, the river below a mirror of gray, its current whispering secrets I couldn’t hear. The air was thick with the scent of wet earth and old wood, and every step felt like a struggle—my breath shallow, my heart heavy with the weight of the world.  \n\nThe bridge was a relic of a bygone era, its planks worn by time and tide. I passed by the old mill, where generations had fought for a better life, their struggles etched into the stone. The river, though still, carried the echoes of those who had dared to dream beyond the confines of their small towns.  \n\nI paused at the edge, staring into the water, where the light of the sun danced on the surface like a fleeting dream. My breath caught in my throat, and for a moment, I wondered if the river would ever let me go.",
